/*
  # base-uri is 'self', not 'none': /demo, /originate and /receive are
  # real directories serving a copy of index.html that carries
  # <base href="/"> so its relative assets still resolve from the root.
  # 'none' blocked that tag outright, so every asset resolved against
  # /demo/, 404ed into HTML and was rejected on MIME type - the whole
  # page rendered unstyled with no script. 'self' still stops an
  # injected base pointing at another origin, which is what the
  # directive is actually for.
  # The three Google origins are GA4 and nothing else: googletagmanager
  # serves gtag.js, and the analytics hosts receive the measurement calls.
  # Added 9 Sep 2026 with the modem data stream. Before this the page
  # loaded no third-party resource at all, which is worth knowing if the
  # analytics ever come back out - the policy should come out with them.
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.googletagmanager.com; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.googletagmanager.com; media-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), microphone=(self)
  # Everything revalidates before it is reused.
  #
  # Cloudflare Pages' own default for .js and .css is `public,
  # max-age=14400, must-revalidate` - four hours in the *browser* cache -
  # while it serves HTML and .wasm at `max-age=0`. Nothing on this site
  # carries a content hash in its filename, so those four hours mean a
  # returning visitor gets today's HTML wired to yesterday's JavaScript.
  # The deploy's edge purge cannot help: it clears Cloudflare's copy, not
  # the one already on the visitor's disk.
  #
  # That is not hypothetical. The Demo button went on 404ing for
  # `modem.wasm` after the fix for it was live and verified correct at
  # the origin, because the browser kept running a cached `wired.js` that
  # still resolved the URL the old way. It cost most of an afternoon,
  # because the deployed bytes and the running bytes were different
  # things and every check of the former said the site was fine.
  #
  # `no-cache` does not mean "do not store". It means "store it, but
  # always revalidate before reuse", so the ordinary case is a 304 with
  # no body - and the ETags already exist. It is set here on `/*` rather
  # than on `/*.js` and `/*.css`, which is where it was tried first:
  # Pages' wildcard is a path splat, not a glob, so a suffix pattern
  # silently matches nothing. Measured directly - the rule deployed and
  # .js kept coming back max-age=14400.
  #
  # The better answer for the code is hashed filenames plus `immutable`,
  # which needs a build step this site's plain JS does not have. This is
  # the honest version of the same guarantee rather than a pretence of
  # one, and the whole site is a few hundred kilobytes, so the round
  # trips it costs are not the problem worth optimising.
  Cache-Control: no-cache
